<article class="page-prose"><section id="available" class="prose-section"><h2>Available publications</h2><p>This page brings together the programme’s published framework and related foundational work. Further research publications will be added as they are released.</p></section><section id="specification" class="prose-section"><h2>Galapagensis Technical Specification</h2><p><em>Method and Data Model for Relational Documentary Research in Galápagos History, Knowledge and Memory</em></p><p>Edgardo Civallero · 2026 · Version 1.4</p><p>The methodological and data-model framework for connecting dispersed sources, documenting evidence-backed relationships, preserving uncertainty and tracing how historical knowledge is produced.</p><p>DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.22816706 · CC BY-NC-ND 4.0</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22816706">Read and download from Zenodo</a></p></section><section id="foundation" class="prose-section"><h2>Related foundational work</h2><h3><em>Los tejedores de memorias</em></h3><p>Edgardo Civallero · 2023 · Thesis · Spanish</p><p>The thesis develops the epistemic framework underlying Galapagensis: documentary work as the recovery, connection, interpretation and activation of heterogeneous fragments of memory and knowledge. It predates the independent programme.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19054301">Read the thesis on Zenodo</a></p></section><section id="working" class="prose-section"><h2>Working documentation</h2><p>The Production Data Architecture v0.3, Domain & Vocabulary Framework v0.2, Website Architecture & Design Blueprint v0.3 and Research Agenda v0.1 support the programme’s development. This list identifies working documents; it does not announce public releases or provide downloads that are not yet available here.</p><p><a href="/research-agenda/">Read the public Research Agenda</a></p></section><section id="future" class="prose-section"><h2>Publication horizons</h2><p>Planned forms include research monographs, recovered historical texts, critical editions, documentary compilations, photographic and thematic books, scholarly articles and educational resources. These are publication intentions, rather than a catalogue of completed titles.</p></section><section id="offline" class="prose-section"><h2>Galapagensis to go</h2><p>The offline-access programme is intended for readers, schools and communities with limited or unreliable connectivity. Future resources may include PDFs, EPUBs, print-friendly teaching materials and thematic packages derived from the same research corpus. No offline packages are offered on this page yet.</p></section><section id="reuse" class="prose-section"><h2>Citation and reuse</h2><p>Use the DOI and version when citing the Technical Specification. For each publication, consult its own rights and licence notice. The language of this page does not imply that the linked publication has been translated.</p><p><a href="/rights-and-use/">Rights, Licensing & Use</a></p></section></article></div></section>
